# Summary of changes for run efe45c78-8060-47aa-bb8d-2240d5381b97
Completed a full Phase A research cycle on the Collatz (3n+1) conjecture, delivering three fully-proved Lean 4 files plus the required research documents.

Deliverables (all main theorems proved with 0 sorries; verified to depend only on the standard axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound):

1. `Catalog/Applications/Collatz/StoppingTime.lean` — category: subtask of the open Collatz problem. Defines the standard map `C` and shortcut map `T`, and proves:
   - `pow_two_reaches_one`: every power of two reaches 1 in exactly its exponent many standard steps (by induction);
   - `T_step_mod_four`: the exact two-step shortcut image `T (T (4k+1)) = 3k+1`;
   - `mod_four_one_drops`: every n ≡ 1 (mod 4) with n > 1 strictly decreases after two shortcut steps — an unconditional finite stopping-time bound for a positive-density residue class.

2. `Catalog/Applications/Collatz/CycleObstruction.lean` — category: subtask of the open Collatz problem. Proves:
   - `T_no_fixed_point`: no positive period-1 cycle;
   - `T_lt_of_even` / `T_gt_of_odd`: the even-shrinks/odd-grows dichotomy;
   - `all_even_descent`: along an all-even run, `T^[k] n = n / 2^k` (by induction);
   - `periodic_has_odd`: every positive periodic point of the shortcut map has an odd number in its orbit (no purely-even cycle).

3. `Catalog/Bridges/CollatzTwoAdic.lean` — category: cross-domain bridge (Applications/Collatz ↔ NumberTheory / p-adic valuation). Defines the accelerated odd map and proves:
   - `accel_factorization` and `accel_padic_factorization`: `3n+1 = 2^{v₂} · accelOdd n`;
   - `accelOdd_odd`: the accelerated odd map always lands in the odd numbers;
   - `v2_eq_padic`: the dynamical halving count equals Mathlib's `padicValNat 2` (the exact Collatz ↔ 2-adic bridge);
   - `v2_odd_pos`: positivity of the valuation on odd inputs.

Each `.lean` file contains the required `-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--` blocks documenting the Hypothesize/Experiment/Analyze/Critique/Synthesize loop. Also added `Catalog/Applications/Collatz/FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` (four bold, falsifiable conjectures, each with a "The key insight is..." sentence and a "Why now?" justification, all derived from this cycle's findings) and `Catalog/Applications/Collatz/ComputationalEvidence.md` (small-case tables and OEIS notes motivating the theorems).

Notes on the project: the repository's `lakefile.toml` default targets point at root directories (e.g. `Algebra`) while all sources live under `Catalog/`, so the pre-existing project does not build as a whole; this state was left unchanged. The new files are self-contained (`import Mathlib`) and were verified to elaborate and prove cleanly through the Lean toolchain. They extend the existing catalog Collatz material (`Cryptography.CollatzHash`, `MachineLearning.Cycles`) conceptually, with the relationship documented in the docstrings and Lab Notes; cross-catalog `import` was not used because the catalog libraries are not wired into the build.
